From 3a908edc7c5682aa5f034c7ad77a34c6e1759da1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:39:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] StaticMemPool: zero only the pages handed out, not the whole
 pool

clear() memset the entire pages array, and every instance of this
template is a namespace-scope global whose constructor runs before main.
So each process started by writing 1.05 GiB of zeroes over .bss that the
loader had already zeroed -- weaponMemPool 758 MiB, projMemPool 142,
unitMemPool 138, featureMemPool 45 -- and held every page of it resident
for its whole life, whatever the size of the game being simulated.

The pool's invariant is that an unallocated page reads as zero. allocMem
hands pages out in order and freeMem zeroes each one it takes back, so
everything past used_page_count is already zero and only the used prefix
can be dirty. Zeroing that prefix keeps the invariant exactly; at
construction it is empty, so the pools now cost what their live objects
cost.

Headless BAR re-simulation on a 7.9 GB host, 8v8 replay: peak RSS was
6.7 GB and the run was stopped for want of memory at 95% of the demo.
---
 rts/System/MemPoolTypes.h | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rts/System/MemPoolTypes.h b/rts/System/MemPoolTypes.h
index 34e0824..57b883a 100644
--- a/rts/System/MemPoolTypes.h
+++ b/rts/System/MemPoolTypes.h
@@ -354,7 +354,21 @@ public:
 
 	void reserve(size_t) {} // no-op
 	void clear() {
-		std::memset(pages.data(), 0, total_size());
+		// Only the pages that were ever handed out can be dirty: allocMem walks
+		// `pages` in order and freeMem zeroes every page it takes back, so the
+		// tail past used_page_count still reads as zero and re-zeroing it here
+		// buys nothing. Writing the whole array instead is what made the four
+		// static pools resident in full from the first instant of the process
+		// (weapon 758 MiB + projectile 142 + unit 138 + feature 45 = ~1.05 GiB
+		// of .bss, all of it zeroes) on every run, whatever the size of the
+		// game -- and this construction runs before main, so a headless replay
+		// paid it before it knew which demo it was about to simulate.
+		//
+		// The pool's own invariant, "an unallocated page reads as zero", is
+		// what makes this safe, and it holds from the start because every
+		// instance of this template is a namespace-scope global: .bss is
+		// zero-filled by the loader, so the constructor has nothing to do.
+		std::memset(pages.data(), 0, used_page_count * PAGE_SIZE());
 		std::memset(indcs.data(), 0, NUM_PAGES());
 
 		used_page_count = 0;
-- 
